    "root_rendered_source": "parent messages and parent-owned ongoing/root_landing_qa receipt; not replayed by this subagent",
    "observation": "Localized footer headings expose malformed translation identifiers and Translation missing text. This is not an HTTP/empty collection finding.",
    "cause_level": "INFERRED_FROM_PUBLIC_OUTPUT_PLUS_REPO_CODE; exact current MAIN Liquid and admin translation records were not freshly queried",
    "mechanism": "Local footer passes arbitrary block.settings.heading with t: into the translation filter and otherwise prints the literal. Canonical English block tokens are non-display identifiers that appear to have been translated in localized theme settings. Existing correct ro locale values therefore can be bypassed. Candidate hardening recognizes only two Danish aliases plus English/Danish key/error prefixes; malformed unprefixed RO/NL/DE/EL names can survive those checks.",
    "proposed_fix": "Owning UX operator should first bind the current candidate/footer source and exact three localized heading records to the verified public failures. Preserve identifiers, resolve the three known footer roles to canonical translation keys, and repair only proved malformed localized heading values/aliases. Keep intentional custom literal/rich-text headings and unrelated block/menu settings unchanged. Add current RO/NL/DE/EL/FI failures to existing EN/ES/DA holdouts. Do not mass-remove admin translations.",
    "locale_content_limit": "Root and candidate nl footer_headings values are English; removing raw-key leakage alone does not establish native Dutch quality. Existing ro canonical values are readable Romanian in local source but no native-language certification is implied.",
    "approval_and_ownership": "Proposal only; UX task01a088c3 owns implementation and publication gates. No shared theme, locale or admin field changed."
  },
